{"title":"Career Roadmap · Doctor / Medical Officer","role":"Doctor / Medical Officer","summary":"A Doctor / Medical Officer is a qualified medical professional who evaluates patients, identifies or manages health conditions within their scope of practice, provides treatment, coordinates care and promotes preventive health.","facts":{"Current degree":"MBBS (Bachelor of Medicine & Bachelor of Surgery)","Course":"MBBS"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Doctor / Medical Officer is a qualified medical professional who evaluates patients, identifies or manages health conditions within their scope of practice, provides treatment, coordinates care and promotes preventive health."},{"type":"p","text":"An MBBS graduate can work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Clinics"},{"text":"Primary healthcare"},{"text":"Community health"},{"text":"Emergency services"},{"text":"Government health services"},{"text":"Corporate healthcare"},{"text":"Occupational health"},{"text":"Public-health programmes"},{"text":"Medical research"},{"text":"Healthcare administration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The MBBS pathway is different from most undergraduate careers because the degree alone is not the entire professional pathway. The student must complete the applicable compulsory internship, registration and other regulatory requirements before practicing independently as permitted under current rules."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12 – PCB","NEET-UG / Applicable Medical Admission Route","MBBS","Clinical Training","Compulsory Rotatory Internship","Medical Registration","Doctor / Medical Officer","Experience / Specialization","Senior Medical Officer / Specialist / Medical Administrator"]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["MBBS","Compulsory Internship","Medical Registration","PG Entrance / Applicable Ad